Z||000006||firstfiero||09-17-2001||10:24 PM||||        Father in law wrecked his 90 corvette convertable a few years ago. The road was to split to the left or right..... he went straight. speed was about 120 mph. Launched the car into the air as it came down the rear wheels clipped a small wall in front of a grassy area. That sent him into a end over end flip and that's when the rolling began. . Vette was demo'd of course. The front clip was gone. The tranny smashed through the fire wall. And the 2 grand he had spent on tires were nothing but scraps of what was left of the rims. Oh by the way he got a chipped tooth and broke his glasses.....lucky bastard.    <P>------------------<BR><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/firstfiero.gif"> ||||reg||14
